  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Installing a new bathroom vanity is a great way to refresh your space, and knowing the steps involved can help you prepare. First up, we'll take careful measurements of your space and pinpoint where your rough plumbing is located. This ensures your new vanity will fit perfectly and aligns with your water lines. Then, it's time to remove the old vanity unit, sink, and faucet. This can get a little messy, but we keep things tidy. Once the old unit is out, we set and level the new vanity cabinet. This is crucial for a stable, professional look, especially if your floor isn't perfectly even. After the cabinet is in place, we reconnect the sink and faucet to your plumbing. This is where precision matters to prevent leaks! Finally, we'll add any finishing touches like trim, install your chosen countertop, and caulk around the edges for a clean, watertight seal. The main thing to remember is coordination; ensuring the plumbing and countertop work together smoothly makes all the difference. For a hassle-free vanity installation, HH Remodeling LLC is ready to help. Call us at 303-505-0866."
    }
  ],
